- **`/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/MCP-Auto-Server/src/server.ts`** -- The core MCP server definition. It:
  - Creates a `Server` instance from `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` (NOT FastMCP -- it uses the raw SDK directly)
  - Registers tool handlers for: `add_config`, `update_and_validate_config`, `execute_command`, `validate_config`, `need_use_these_tools`
  - Uses Zod schemas from `/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/MCP-Auto-Server/src/tools/schemas.ts`

- **Compiled output**: `/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/MCP-Auto-Server/dist/index.js` (the runnable entry point)

### Python Automation Agent (mcp-auto)

- **`/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp-auto/1-auto_mcp_deploy.py`** -- Main automation script that:
  - Connects to multiple MCP servers listed in `mcp_server_config.json`
  - Uses an LLM (Qwen via DashScope API) with tool-calling loop to automatically analyze READMEs and deploy MCP servers
  - Implements a phase-based workflow: analyze -> deploy -> validate -> fix

- **`/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp-auto/MCP_hub.py`** -- An interactive MCP host/chat interface that connects to one MCP server and provides a chat loop with LLM tool calling

- **`/home/silimon/MCP-Auto/mcp-auto/MCP_Client.py`** -- MCP client implementation supporting stdio, SSE, and streamable HTTP connections

